# The warning about an empty send belongs to the empty message. Send with
# nothing typed stays on the message, and once a letter is typed the
# warning no longer describes what is in the box.
wait 800
tap-id kb.backspace
tap-id kb.backspace
tap-id kb.backspace
tap Send
wait-for There is nothing here to send.
expect-missing Stop
expect one second of light
type t
expect 3 seconds to send.
clean
shot typed-after-empty
expect-missing There is nothing here to send.
# A character with no code is named while it is in the box, and the
# warning goes with it.
tap ?123
wait 200
type !
expect Morse has no code for !
tap-id kb.backspace
expect-missing Morse has no code for
# After a send, Edit returns to the message without the beacon's warning
# about the character it left out, once that character is gone.
type !
tap Send
wait-for so it was left out.
tap Stop
wait-for Send again
tap Edit
wait-for one second of light
tap-id kb.backspace
expect-missing Morse has no code for
clean
shot warning-gone
